 "text": "Hello there, how are you? That's a common problem. One way to fix it is to draw a thin line under each eye hole, and then fill in the middle part with a broad pen. Fill in the outside with a thin pen to make it look solid. Whichever you choose, always draw a line under each eyehole before filling in the outside. Draw each nostril with a separate pen or eyeliner tip, or use a sharp sharp with an automatic pen. It looks much neater than doing each one with the same pen. Enjoying the process is half fun. Whichever you choose, a thin line under the eyes, or drawing each nostril separately, each makes a difference.",
